{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the focus of the parabola given by the equation \\( y = \\frac{5x^2 - 4x + 2}{4} \\), we need to rewrite the equation in the standard form of a parabola that opens upwards or downwards, which is \\( y = a(x-h)^2 + k \\). Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Rewrite the equation in standard form:**\n   Start with the given equation:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5x^2 - 4x + 2}{4}\n   \\]\n   Rewrite it as:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}x^2 - \\frac{4}{4}x + \\frac{2}{4}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the coefficients:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}x^2 - x + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Complete the square for the \\(x\\)-terms:**\n   To complete the square, we focus on the first two terms: \\( \\frac{5}{4}x^2 - x \\).\n   Factor out \\(\\frac{5}{4}\\) from the \\(x\\)-terms:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x^2 - \\frac{4}{5}x\\right) + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   To complete the square inside the parentheses, take half of the coefficient of \\(x\\), which is \\(-\\frac{4}{5}\\), divide by 2 to get \\(-\\frac{2}{5}\\), and then square it to get \\(\\left(-\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{4}{25}\\). Add and subtract \\(\\frac{4}{25}\\) inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x^2 - \\frac{4}{5}x + \\frac{4}{25} - \\frac{4}{25}\\right) + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   Rewrite the expression inside the parentheses as a perfect square:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(\\left(x - \\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 - \\frac{4}{25}\\right) + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   Distribute \\(\\frac{5}{4}\\):\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x - \\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 - \\frac{5}{4} \\cdot \\frac{4}{25} + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the constant term:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x - \\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 - \\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   Find a common denominator to combine the constant terms:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x - \\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 - \\frac{2}{10} + \\frac{5}{10}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the constant terms:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{5}{4}\\left(x - \\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 + \\frac{3}{10}\n   \\]\n   Now the equation is in the standard form \\( y = a(x-h)^2 + k \\), where \\( a = \\frac{5}{4} \\), \\( h = \\frac{2}{5} \\), and \\( k = \\frac{3}{10} \\).\n\n","prefix_end":2025,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,5244,315,279,1346,370,7924,2661,553,279,23606,17767,379,284,1124,37018,90,20,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,220,17,15170,19,92,1124,701,582,1184,311,18130,279,23606,304,279,5297,1352,315,264,1346,370,7924,429,15885,43954,476,91270,11,892,374,17767,379,284,264,2075,2832,29776,17,488,595,1124,568,5692,525,279,7354,1447,16,13,3070,58465,1247,279,23606,304,5297,1352,25,1019,256,5145,448,279,2661,23606,510,256,1124,9640,256,379,284,1124,37018,90,20,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,220,17,15170,19,532,256,1124,921,256,93213,432,438,510,256,1124,9640,256,379,284,1124,37018,90,20,15170,19,92,87,61,17,481,1124,37018,90,19,15170,19,92,87,488,1124,37018,90,17,15170,19,532,256,1124,921,256,61242,1437,279,36829,510,256,1124,9640,256,379,284,1124,37018,90,20,15170,19,92,87,61,17,481,856,488,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,532,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,12548,279,9334,369,279,17767,87,59,7287,18347,25,1019,256,2014,4583,279,9334,11,582,5244,389,279,1156,1378,3793,25,17767,1124,37018,90,20,15170,19,92,87,61,17,481,856,1124,4292,256,37729,700,1124,11520,37018,90,20,15170,19,11035,8,504,279,17767,87,59,7287,18347,510,256,1124,9640,256,379,284,1124,37018,90,20,15170,19,11035,2359,2075,61,17,481,1124,37018,90,19,15170,20,92,87,59,1291,8,488,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,532,256,1124,921,256,2014,4583,279,9334,4766,279,73975,11,1896,4279,315,279,35606,315,17767,87,59,701,892,374,1124,4080,59,37018,90,19,15170,20,11035,701,21749,553,220,17,311,633,1124,4080,59,37018,90,17,15170,20,11035,701,323,1221,9334,432,311,633,1124,11520,2359,4080,59,37018,90,17,15170,20,11035,1291,29776,17,284,1124,37018,90,19,